## Approval and cost

- Before multiple paid generations, show the effective image, video, scene, and variant counts and the known approval points.
- Before approval, produce only the brief, plan, prompt, layout, or web handoff that the user requested.
- Never claim a connected-tool or web-only action completed unless it actually completed and can be verified.
- Record approvals and reversals in `.chany-studio/state.md` without upgrading an unknown value to approved.

## Quality gate

- Compare product shape, count, color, material, label, logo, model identity, garment structure, and approved copy against their authority sources.
- Check channel ratio, safe area, mobile readability, CTA, language, and campaign-family consistency.
- Reject unapproved claims, fabricated details, unintended source changes, broken copy, and unverifiable completion.
- Name observed defects and the smallest repair path. Use `chany-image-edit` only for a bounded change to an accepted image.

## Files and handoff

- Keep source files separate from drafts and finals. Use descriptive names containing deliverable, ratio or size, language when relevant, and revision.
- Do not overwrite an approved final. Create a new revision and update the output index in `.chany-studio/state.md`.
- Store no passwords, API keys, access tokens, cookies, signed URLs, temporary download URLs, or hidden credentials.
- Explicit instructions in the current conversation override this file.
